    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a soft slate against weak opposing arms today, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leading the charge at a 74.56 efficiency rating. He is our strongest play, bolstered by an ideal matchup against Young, whose 4.77 xERA provides a massive boost to our middle infield production. **Josh Lowe** (72.21) and **Nolan Schanuel** (67.16) similarly benefit from facing Sasaki\u2019s 5.23 xERA; the optimizer heavily favors this stack as we hunt for counting stats. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a slight platoon disadvantage against Lovelady, his underlying talent remains high enough to warrant a 62.99 start, and we continue to prioritize the speed profile of **Nasim Nunez**, whose high SP-skill projection keeps him in the lineup despite a sub-optimal batting order position.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision today involved **Coby Mayo**, whose 57.80 score narrowly missed the cut behind the high-efficiency ceiling of our primary outfielders. While **Coby Mayo** offers intrigue, the sheer volume of favorable SP matchups for our starters pushed him to the bench. We are also closely monitoring the lineup status of **Jackson Merrill**; if the pending lineup shifts him out of the lead-off spot, his current 56.83 score\u2014already depressed by a tough test against George Kirby\u2014could drop further. Conversely, **Liam Hicks** carries a 45.47 risk profile due to Rasmussen\u2019s efficiency, but he remains in the C2 slot as our most viable option for plate appearances today. We enter this contest with a high confidence in our core of **Drake Baldwin**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Dominic Smith**, **Brady House**, and **Andy Pages** to navigate the daily efficiency targets.",
